Add skipIgnition to the commpage dyld_flags before launchd is exec'd.

The stock iOS 16.6 dyld-1066 probes libignition first; without kernel-side
ignition support it comes back with a cache fd that does not resolve to our
on-disk cache, and launchd dies on the missing libSystem.  Setting
dyld_flags=0x8 (skipIgnition) makes dyld fall through to the plain system
cache directory instead.
---
--- a/bsd/kern/kern_exec.c
+++ b/bsd/kern/kern_exec.c
@@ -6879,6 +6879,18 @@
 	mach_vm_offset_t scratch_addr = 0;
 	mach_vm_size_t map_page_size = vm_map_page_size(map);
 
+#if defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_LIUQIN)
+	{
+		/* LIUQIN: there is no kernel-side ignition support, and the
+		 * stock dyld probes it first, fails with a NULL cache dir and
+		 * dies on the missing libSystem.  Skip it and let dyld fall
+		 * through to the on-disk cache in /System/Library/Caches. */
+		extern void commpage_update_dyld_flags(uint64_t);
+		commpage_update_dyld_flags(0x8); /* skipIgnition */
+		printf("LIUQIN: commpage dyld_flags=skipIgnition\n");
+	}
+#endif
+
 	(void) mach_vm_allocate_kernel(map, &scratch_addr, map_page_size, VM_FLAGS_ANYWHERE, VM_KERN_MEMORY_NONE);
 #if CONFIG_MEMORYSTATUS
 	(void) memorystatus_init_at_boot_snapshot();
